## 1. Set Up Ubuntu 20.04 LTS with Kernel 5.8 in QEMU

### a) Download Ubuntu 20.04 LTS Cloud Image

```bash
wget https://cloud-images.ubuntu.com/focal/current/focal-server-cloudimg-amd64.img
```

### b) Download Linux Kernel 5.8

Ubuntu 20.04 ships with kernel 5.4 by default. We will install a custom kernel 5.8.

- Download kernel 5.8 from kernel.ubuntu.com or kernel.org:

```bash
mkdir kernel5.8 && cd kernel5.8
wget https://kernel.ubuntu.com/~kernel-ppa/mainline/v5.8/amd64/linux-headers-5.8.0-050800-generic_5.8.0-050800.202008302330_amd64.deb
wget https://kernel.ubuntu.com/~kernel-ppa/mainline/v5.8/amd64/linux-image-unsigned-5.8.0-050800-generic_5.8.0-050800.202008302330_amd64.deb
